DOM MANIPULATION – INSERT & DELETE ELEMENTS

DOM = Document Object Model.
It allows JavaScript to CREATE, ADD, and REMOVE HTML elements dynamically.

1. CREATE AN ELEMENT
   let el = document.createElement("div");

   → Creates a new <div> element.
   → It is created in memory, but NOT yet visible on the webpage.

   Example:
   let el = document.createElement("div");
   el.textContent = "Hello";


2. APPEND – Add at the END (inside)
   node.append(el);

   If HTML is:
   <div id="box">
       <p>First</p>
   </div>

   After:
   box.append(el);

   Result:
   <div id="box">
       <p>First</p>
       <div>Hello</div>   ← added at the END
   </div>


3. PREPEND – Add at the START (inside)
   node.prepend(el);

   Result:
   <div id="box">
       <div>Hello</div>   ← added at the START
       <p>First</p>
   </div>


4. BEFORE – Add BEFORE the node (outside)
   node.before(el);

   If:
   <div id="box">Box</div>

   Result:
   <div>Hello</div>       ← added before the box
   <div id="box">Box</div>


5. AFTER – Add AFTER the node (outside)
   node.after(el);

   Result:
   <div id="box">Box</div>
   <div>Hello</div>       ← added after the box


6. REMOVE – Delete the node
   node.remove();

   Example:
   let box = document.getElementById("box");
   box.remove();

   → Completely removes the element from the webpage.


EASY WAY TO REMEMBER:

   createElement() → CREATE a new element

   append()        → ADD inside, at END
   prepend()       → ADD inside, at START
   before()        → ADD outside, BEFORE
   after()         → ADD outside, AFTER
   remove()        → DELETE the element


COMPLETE EXAMPLE:

   let box = document.getElementById("box");

   let el = document.createElement("div");
   el.textContent = "Hello World";

   box.append(el);      // inside, end
   box.prepend(el);     // inside, start
   box.before(el);      // before box
   box.after(el);       // after box
   el.remove();         // delete el


IMPORTANT:
   createElement() = CREATE
   append/prepend/before/after = ADD
   remove() = DELETE